{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791570744,"nonce":"O9NY8MmOaY7q+XJsqcCrs88GSFI=","title":"Watches and computeds each hold a GC root and a boxed closure natively","message":"Each Watch passes its read closure to blinc_abi's hl_blinc_effect, which roots it (hl::Rooted, an hl_add_root slot), wraps it in a boxed Rust closure calling back through hl_dyn_call, and returns a finalizer handle. Blinc's graph calls each due effect into Haxe one at a time from its own flush. Computeds are held the same way (hl_blinc_computed_*). Blinc is adding host-run effects (blinc_core 44653b4b, Blinc git-bug 1b04867, not yet pushed when filed): an effect with no closure, a pull of due effect ids, and begin_host_effect/end_host_effect to run host code under tracking on the global graph. With them a Watch is an id; Haxe runs the due watches' reads and reactions in one pass.\n\n**Baseline** (2026-10-09, Ash release at ded1b08+, M-series Mac; a program making N items under an Owner and reading each computed once, then disposing; process footprint with footprint -p and Ash's GC heap from hl.Gc.stats, first round of 30,000 items, per item):\n- signal: 907 B footprint, 116 B GC heap\n- computed: 1,377 B footprint, 298 B GC heap\n- watch: 1,643 B footprint, 599 B GC heap\nLater rounds reuse that memory, so the first round is the cost of making them.\n\n**Also found:** disposing N computeds that read one signal is quadratic in blinc_core (dispose_derived removes from the signal's subscriber list with retain): 100,000 computeds were still disposing after 14 minutes. Reported to blinc-b1. A shared signal (theme, scheme) read by every element's bindings makes unmounting a large list quadratic.\n\n**Then:** blinc_abi's HashLink exports for host effects; Watch keeps its read and react in Haxe by id, run from LayoutTree.flush in one pass; measure again with the same program.","files":null}]}